sts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NuojCheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/33204220590/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/33204220590/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/check-suites/89992220479","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/33204220590/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/33204220590/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/33204220590/rerun","previous_attempt_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/runs/33204220590/attempts/1","workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext/actions/workflows/297948505","head_commit":{"id":"d5679bfc7f4c7917f1cf17eb994cd298d89b33a0","tree_id":"a9f7411e330fb20b0d979c9da64b79984b982a3f","message":"Address review on the GatedDeltaNet context-parallel scan\n\ncontext_parallel_load_balance defaults to true and reorders the batch\nDUAL_CHUNK_SWAP at ctx>1: device 0 takes the first and last chunk, device 1\nthe second and second-to-last. Softmax attention survives that because it\nrebuilds the causal mask from positions. The GatedDeltaNet layers carry a\nrecurrence, so device order is sequence order and the reorder composes the\nsegments out of order. The run still trains and the loss still falls, so\nconfigs/types.py raises rather than warns. Thanks to @NuojCheng for catching\nit.\n\nAlso from review:\n\n- gdn_cp.py moves to kernels/attention/, beside the other collectives (@darisoy)\n- lax.axis_size replaces the all-gather that computed the device count\n- one gdn_context_axes() helper replaces the same expression at three sites\n- the docstring pointed at apply_gdn_context_parallel.py, which is not in this\n  repo. It carries the derivation instead\n\nThe tests covered the forward pass only, so they gain two things.\n\nGradient checks. gdn_cp defines no custom_vjp, so the backward is whatever\nJAX's transpose rules for lax.scan, lax.ppermute and lax.psum compose into. A\nppermute transposes to the inverse permutation, so a cotangent has to travel\nback down the rank chain for an early shard to see any gradient from a late\none. Worst relative error against the sequential recurrence is 2.3e-07 on an\n8-device CPU mesh, and every rank sees gradient.\n\nAn end-to-end check, which @NuojCheng asked for. It runs\njax_chunk_gated_delta_rule itself, sharded against unsharded, and catches a\nwrong chunk layout or a wrong replay. Two config tests cover the load-balance\nrejection and the build with it off.","timestamp":"2026-08-28T19:30:57Z","author":{"name":"Willis Zhang","email":"williszhang@google.com"},"committer":{"name":"Willis Zhang","email":"williszhang@google.com"}},"repository":{"id":607845880,"node_id":"R_kgDOJDr9-A","name":"maxtext","full_name":"AI-Hypercomputer/maxtext","private":false,"owner":{"login":"AI-Hypercomputer","id":181000646,"node_id":"O_kgDOCsnZxg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181000646?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Hypercomputer","html_url":"https://github.com/AI-Hypercomputer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Hypercomputer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Hypercomputer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AI-Hyper